' ── DEVICES, SESSION, AND BROWSER ───────────────────────────────────────────
' The devices row packs android and ios into consecutive columns. Android is
' selectable and ios is disabled pending implementation. A harness with no
' mobile devices omits the row.
' A harness with Desktop offers tui and desktop as radio choices on a session
' row. Other harnesses use the terminal session implicitly. The selected
' Desktop option enters the add-on list; tui is the default.
' The browser row offers off, isolated, named, and host according to capability.
' Isolated uses a disposable sandbox profile. Named reveals the profile-name
' field. Host selects the existing Chrome add-on.
' Pinned by TestTheDevicesRowPacksItsOptionsWithoutGaps,
' TestTUIAndDesktopAreOneRadioChoice (internal/run) and
' TestARadioSetDrawsRadiosBesideCheckboxes (internal/choiceui).
