' ── THE AUTH ROW IS AN AXIS, AND IT IS ORDERED BY RISK ─────────────────────
' Three options, always drawn in this order, because the prompt labels the row's
' horizontal as "◀ riskier ... safer ▶" and reading it left to right has to mean
' something:
'   usage credits ... metered per token against raw provider key material sitting
'                     in the environment for the agent to read. Unbounded spend,
'                     and the key is a file or a variable the agent can reach.
'   subscription .... a fixed-cost plan credential, and where it is a login on
'                     disk proveo suppresses env tokens over it. The failure this
'                     row exists to stop runs one way only — a subscription run
'                     silently billed per token, never the reverse.
'   local model ..... the safe end. Weights on this machine: nothing billed, and
'                     no credential for the agent or the egress hop to carry.
'                     COMING SOON — `--local-model` already runs the Ollama
'                     sidecar, but nothing routes THIS row to it, so it is drawn
'                     and gated rather than left out. The axis is where an
'                     operator looks to find out an option exists.
' Egress columns run riskier to safer. Model columns follow the credential
' inventory for cloud choices, then show local choices.
'
' AN UNAVAILABLE OPTION IS GATED, NEVER DROPPED. cursor's CLI has no
' bring-your-own-key path, so "usage credits" is off with the reason attached —
' dropping it is what made "cursor ignores my ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" something the
' operator could only discover by running. The reason goes in OffWhy, per option,
' so it appears under the option the cursor is on rather than as one row-wide
' string; Reason keeps the joined form for the row.
'
' comingSoon is NOT used here. It reallocates Off on every call, so gating two of
' three through it silently un-gates the first — the auth row gates its own
' options and picks a new Selected when the remembered one landed on a gate.
'
' AND A GATED OPTION ON A SINGLE-SELECT ROW EXPLAINS ITSELF THROUGH Reason, NOT
' OffWhy. cycle() skips an Off option on a single-select row — correctly, it
' cannot be chosen — so the cursor never lands on it and the per-option OffWhy
' is text nothing will ever display. helpLines suppressed the row-level Reason
' the moment the row carried any Help, which is exactly the shape of the auth
' row: cursor drew `usage credits` greyed out and said NOTHING about why, the
' one thing drawing it was supposed to communicate. The egress row escaped this
' only by carrying no Help map.
'
' A Multi row is not affected and keeps its old behaviour: cycle() moves onto
' gated options there and toggle() refuses, so its OffWhy is reachable and
' repeating Reason beside it would double the add-on rows up.
' SUPERSEDED 2026-11-14 (A DISABLED OPTION TAKES THE CURSOR, below): cycle()
' lands on the gated option of a radio row too. Its OffWhy is the status line
' under it; the row's Reason still shows under the options the row can choose.
'
' ── A DISABLED OPTION TAKES THE CURSOR (DECIDED 2026-11-14) ────────────────
' The owner: "always let disabled options be hoverable; the hint should
' explain its status". The keys and the answer: wizard-keys.puml (EVERY
' OPTION TAKES THE CURSOR). This section owns how the hover draws and what
' the help under the card says.
' THE CELLS. The chosen answer keeps (•) and bold (chosen). The hovered
' disabled option draws ( ) in focusOff: black on grey, struck through. No
' other cell changes. Group 13 below draws it.
' THE HELP for a hovered disabled option (Row.unavailable: off, not in
' force, on an unlocked row):
'   › <option> — <Help>     the head; "› <option>" alone without Help
'   off: <OffWhy>           the status (Row.status)
' Without an OffWhy the status is the row's Reason; with neither it reads
' "off: not supported on this run" (offUnnamed). An open list's off entry
' without an OffWhy reads the same. A ticked off option keeps "always on:
' <OffWhy>". A locked row keeps its Reason first; that Reason is its status,
' so it adds no "off:" line.
' A LOCKED ROW (verifier pass, 2026-11-14). Every cell of a locked row counts
' as disabled, so each one names itself and states a status:
'   Reason                  first, the status
'   › <option> — <Help>     the head; "› <option>" alone without Help
' Before, a locked row without Help (egress) showed its Reason alone and never
' named the hovered baseline. A locked row without a Reason reads "off: not
' supported on this run" under each option not in force (Row.inForce); the
' answer in force adds no "off:" line, since it is not off. No run row is
' locked without a Reason today.
' AN OPEN LIST ON A LOCKED ROW (verifier pass, 2026-11-14). The hovered
' element is the list's entry. The help names the entry (moreHelp), then
' adds the row's Reason as its status:
'   › anthropic — configured on the host; read-only
'   host credential inventory; configure with proveo init or the run's .env; …
' Before, moreHelp returned alone and the credentials cell showed no status
' whenever its list held an entry. A list that shows no entry adds nothing.
' COST, MEASURED 2026-11-14. The real run form's help slot already held three
' lines (the credentials Reason wraps to two at 76 columns, plus the head), so
' no run or init golden moved and the run form still needs 13 rows at 80
' columns. The choiceui .env fixture (env_list_test.go envForm) has a
' one-line Reason and no cell Help; its slot grew from one line to two, and
' env-list, env-filter and env-nomatch moved at 80x24 and 120x36. At 80x12
' that fixture leaves no row for its open list (listRoom.place needs four:
' two borders, the filter line, one entry), so
' TestTheOpenListNeverCoversTheTitleItsRowOrTheFoot samples 80x13 where it
' sampled 80x12.
' THE ROW'S REASON (gatesAnOption, until 2026-11-14 unreachableGate). It still
' shows under every option a gated radio row can choose: the glance signal at
' rest. Under the hovered disabled option it shows only when that option has
' no OffWhy, so the status never doubles.
' THE HELP SLOT counts the hover: maxHelpLines and checklistHelpSlot probe
' each option through Row.point, the state ←/→ leave.
' ON A CHECKLIST the help holds two lines (helpMost). cutHelp keeps the first
' help line and puts the first status line second when the cut would drop
' it; a kept line whose next line was dropped ends with ….
' MEASURED 2026-11-14 at 80x24, init page 1, distro package hovered:
'   › distro package — sbx via the host package manager, system-wide — needs…
'   off: not offered — proveo cannot pin a package-manager install; `proveo ini…
' THE DATA, so no status repeats its help:
'   run    authHelp gives an option nothing backs only the head clause of what
'          it is ("metered by the vendor beyond the plan's included usage");
