  ONE row picks the model source (2026-09-27). It merges what used to be two:
  the auth row (""usage credits"" · ""subscription"", drawn for a harness with a
  plan) and the local-model row. ""usage credits"" is drawn as ""API keys"" and
  ""subscription"" as ""plan"", so every harness reads the same cells. A harness
  with no plan (hermes) draws ""API keys | . | Glimmer | Qwen 3.8"" —
  the plan column stays empty.
  The row name occupies 16 columns, marker included. credentials is the
  longest name; 12 would put its last letter on the first option.
  Every option row pins to the same four columns. OS, outputs, ports and apps
  included: a missing value leaves its column blank. A cell is at most 10 runes,
  plus a trailing "" (N)"" count (2026-11-14). ""docker (sandbox)"" paints ""sandbox"".
  Model API keys aligns with credential API keys in column 1.
  Plan aligns with OAuth in column 2. Glimmer and Qwen take columns 3 and 4
  from 24 GiB up to 96 GiB of installed accelerator memory.
  At 96 GiB and above, Nemotron and Flash Next take those columns.
  Below 24 GiB, the local columns hold an explicit model when supplied.
  A rule below the choices labels the occupied cloud and local column spans.
  The rule reads ""local (needs 24 GB VRAM)"" or ""local (96 GB VRAM tier)"".
  Apple silicon names unified memory. Flash Next's hint recommends 128 GB.
  The label shares the model row's scrolling span and takes no cursor stop.
  An explicit or remembered model outside the capacity tier follows the pair
  and extends the local rule.
  The inventory uses API keys, OAuth, SSH and .env in columns 1, 2, 3 and 4.
  The pitch shrinks with the card (2026-11-13): 22 columns from a 120-column
  card down to 16 at 80, where column 4 starts at 66.
  27B and 30B live in the hint. Glimmer's hint still says Muse Glimmer.
  GGUF and MLX are the hint, not the label:
  darwin/arm64 says MLX (""qwen3.8:27b-mlx"", ""muse-glimmer:30b-mlx""), every
  other host says GGUF (""qwen3.8:latest"", ""muse-glimmer:latest"").
  Picking one on a plan harness also
  answers auth = ""local model"", which withholds the plan credential.
  ""--local-model <tag>"" preselects the option whose Ollama repo owns the tag and,
